<title>USA: French Fragrances Inc Q3 shr increases.</title>
<headline>French Fragrances Inc Q3 shr increases.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Dollars in Thousands, except share data)</p>
<p>				Three Months Ended  Nine Months Ended</p>
<p>				   October 31,    October 31,</p>
<p>			   1996    1995	  1996	     1995</p>
<p> Net Sales	 $ 60,820 $37,747    $ 103,938	 $ 68,393</p>
<p> Net Earnings	 6,038   2,466	  7,008	    2,505</p>
<p>Primary Earnings</p>
<p>  per Share	  .40(a)  .35(b)	 .54(a)	   .35(b)</p>
<p>Fully Diluted</p>
<p>Earnings per</p>
<p>  Share		   .39  .35(b)	    .53	   .35(b)</p>
<p>Primary Share</p>
<p>Equivalents</p>
<p>		 15,482,717(a)  7,120,000(b) 12,980,052(a)  7,120,000(b)</p>
<p>Fully Diluted</p>
<p>Share</p>
<p>Equivalents</p>
<p>		 15,636,768     7,120,000(b) 13,134,639     7,120,000(b)</p>
<p>NOTE - (a) Primary earnings per share and primary share equivalents give effect to the assumed exercise or conversion of dilutive stock options and convertible securities under the treasury stock method. Based on the actual common shares outstanding, net earnings per share for the three and nine months ended Oct 31, 1996, were $0.46 and $0.63, versus $0.35 and $0.35, respectively, for the comparable periods last year.</p>
<p>(b) Shares for the three and nine months ended October 31, 1995 are presented on a pro forma basis using the conversion factor of 7.12 for each historical share outstanding.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
